{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394665-vicissitude-amalgam-ideas-v5","id":1394665,"title":"Vicissitude Amalgam Ideas (V5)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-06T17:07:17-07:00","id":1394665,"title":"Vicissitude Amalgam Ideas (V5)","content":"So we know per Chicago by night, Tzimisce have Protean, partly because Protean is the discipline of the metamorphic state of vampires. We also know that per the Chicago Folios, they will have blood sorcery in some form as it mentions they have a history of experimenting and creating new rituals. This could be for the kolduns, or it could be for the clan in general. As they are referred to as the Flesh melters, we also know that they still have vicissitude in some form (Either an amalgam, group of them, or possibly even a ritual.)<br /> <br /> At this point the question is how it will be represented in V5? My opinion is that it'll likely be blood sorcery + Protean for most of them, likely using Protean as the main discipline. This serves a few purposes, first it makes Viss something that is already rare, an amalgam, and also combines it with another discipline that is relatively rare, blood sorcery to make it require a teacher. If they remove Auspex, Tzimisce can still survey their land and have eerie knowledge of visitors through blood sorcery rituals and it adds more of a reason behind them still adhering to certain traditions of hospitality.<br /> <br /> Malleable Visage through Bonecraft are likely to be combined into one level 3 amalgam. Chiroptean Marauder could act as a level 5 Amalgam as higher level powers were moved down and an amalgam is a bit more powerful than a usual discipline so using the elder power version would definitely fit. Blood form could also be a level 5 Amalgam, or it could be a blood sorcery amalgam requiring level 5 protean.<br /> <br /> What discipline do you think they'll combine it with and what powers do you think they'll use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T21:20:42-07:00","id":1394716,"title":"","content":"They have been generally good about removing 'baby step' Disciplines. so I wouldn't expect different powers to do flesh and bone separately. I also wouldn't (hopefully) expect a Level 1 power (Malleable Visage) to be as effective as a Level 4 power (Imposter's Guise).<br /> <br /> Basically all they really need is a general fleshcrafting power at 2 or 3 (which can't be as good as mimicking others as Obfuscate 4) and a 'war form' power at 4 to allow for zulo or body armory stuff. The game already allows for refluffs even in the text, so using Feral Weapons for bone spikes and such is fine, and fluffing Mist Form as a bloody mist is fine (Blood Form shouldn't be JUST BETTER than Mist Form for the same level). .<br /> <br /> Personally I want them to keep Auspex in clan and make it Protean/Auspex. Expanded consciousness to 'know' how to shape your own body and then others on a more intrinsic level than Protean makes sense to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}